cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spi in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "spi: Bayesian Spatiotemporal Modelling of Relative Surveillance Reporting"
version: 0.0.0.9000
abstract: >-
  Estimates expected case counts for each district and month using Bayesian
  spatial and temporal models fitted with INLA. The surveillance performance
  index (SPI) compares observed and expected counts, nationally centred by
  default, with credible intervals for uncertainty in expected counts. Tables, maps, and district reports
  support surveillance review.
